{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1415862-oneira-dreamlords-and-adhene","id":1415862,"title":"Oneira, Dreamlords and Adhene","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-28T11:39:54-07:00","id":1415862,"title":"Oneira, Dreamlords and Adhene","content":"Okay I was listening to the Mage Podcast and they talked about the Oneira Dreamlords in 1st ed before Changeling was around. They used to be described as Umbral Lords who went into the dreaming and made homes for themselves by using dreamed up material left by mortals. And I started thinking this would be a good origin for Adhene. Adhene are pretty ambiguous over what makes someone an Adhene rather then some other type of Fae, so what if the secret truth was they were spirits not originating in the Dreaming that went native? They could also represent what Mages encountered and called Oneira when Changelings were stuck in the Autumn World.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I really like the idea of Dreamlords snatching stuff individual dreams and making a home realm out of it, as well as maybe bringing a few things from home(Other Umbrae).<br /> <br /> Changeling didn\u2019t really have much on chimerical Dreamlords, except for a Dragon here and there and maybe some Lost Ones. Changeling the lost was a bit more into that department with Hobgoblins.<br /> <br /> Also I wonder why we don\u2019t have more say Fae souls that stayed in the Near and Far Dreaming rather then going to Arcadia or the Autumn World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T11:46:29-08:00","id":1438151,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve used Oneira before. I basically have them as Dreaming \u2018Incarna\u2019, if you will, effectively omnipotent, but unable to affect the Autumn World or leave the Dreaming. I have it so that Chimera (the tribal totem of the Stargazer werewolves) is a Dream Lord summoned into the Middle Umbra by Gaia.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha de Danaan and the Fomorians were the most <i>powerful</i> Oneira, but far from the only ones. Other Oneira claim to have ruled over Inanimae, Nunnehi, Menehune, Countless and more! They no longer do so (and Menehune and Nunnehi Oneira are effectively unreachable!), claiming a variety of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:02:17-08:00","id":1438382,"title":"","content":"...plus, in Sorcerer, Revised, a hedge mage sect, the Silver Portal, explicitly gets their Paths and rituals from the Oneira.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T16:04:40-08:00","id":1438384,"title":"","content":"I forgot about that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T18:59:23-08:00","id":1438420,"title":"","content":"I also have it where Middle Umbral dream-spirits and Dreaming chimera have \u201cembassies\u201d in each others\u2019 territory, along the Green Roads of Balor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T20:25:37-08:00","id":1438428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1415862-oneira-dreamlords-and-adhene?p=1438420#post1438420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have it where Middle Umbral dream-spirits and Dreaming chimera have \u201cembassies\u201d in each others\u2019 territory, along the Green Roads of Balor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was always a fan of spirit Embassies! I did a thing like that between the Big bads in Malfeas, the Labyrinthe, Yomi and Nightmare. Hoho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T22:38:10-08:00","id":1438437,"title":"","content":"My conception of the Oneira clearly separates them from Fae as the Fae's Dreaming is not directly connected to human (and possibly animal?) dreams. I thought their inspiration seemed more towards Morpheus in Neil Gaiman's Sandman comics. After all, their home is in the Dream Zone, not the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I always felt that the Silver Portal sorcerer group was a call out to Lovecraft's Dreamlands and his mystic dreamers who would visit them. The Silver Port's quest to visit the fabled city of Syrannon reminded me of Randall Carter's dreaming quests. <br /> <br /> This doesn't mean they are completely unrealeted to the Fae and the Dreaming. Morpheus could visit Hell, Asgard, or any number of other domains, so they could do the same. And some connection between the Tuatha de Danaan and the Oneiri is OK.<br /> <br /> My big problem with the Oneiri is that besides Chimera were not given any others. There is a comment in Mage's Book of Worlds that another Oneiri's name is Myathia of the Twelve Collars, but that's it. So I've tried to find other real world myths about the gods of dreams. But besides Morpheus and some other Greek dream gods, there's not a lot. I also raided Marvel Comics to include someone like Nightmare. And I also have an invented Wyrm tainted dream lord to serve as a foil for Chimera. But I would really like a lot more published ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T10:46:45-08:00","id":1438475,"title":"","content":"I avoid Banes and other Wyrmy things, in the Dreaming. In my games, with the exception of the Dauntain, everything fae---<i>including</i> Thallan!---is <i>strictly</i> of the Wyld. Chaos can produce good <i>snd</i> evil, after all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T11:05:04-08:00","id":1438477,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m still on the fence about if Oneira are their own thing or dreaming things viewed by outsiders. Interesting ideas about using Morpheus Black Fox<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1415862-oneira-dreamlords-and-adhene?p=1438475#post1438475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I avoid Banes and other Wyrmy things, in the Dreaming. In my games, with the exception of the Dauntain, everything fae---<i>including</i> Thallan!---is <i>strictly</i> of the Wyld. Chaos can produce good <i>snd</i> evil, after all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah people forget the Zmei started as Wyld creatures after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}